@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-06-09

Feature: Curated Object Paths
  "Normalizes user-assigned share paths and resolves --as / default_path for share uploads."

  Provides:
    - domain.NormalizeObjectPath @source("symbol:NormalizeObjectPath")
    - domain.ResolveSharePath @source("symbol:ResolveSharePath")

  Invariants:
    - Object paths MUST be relative, use forward slashes, and MUST NOT contain ..
    - Paths MUST NOT begin with reserved prefixes .mason/, objects/, or s/
    - ResolveSharePath MUST treat a trailing slash on --as as a directory prefix keeping the local filename

  Scenario (happy-path): Normalize a curated path
    Given a path with backslashes or redundant segments
    When NormalizeObjectPath runs
    Then it returns a canonical forward-slash path

  Scenario (happy-path): Default share placement
    Given an empty --as, a default_path, and a filename
    When ResolveSharePath runs
    Then it places the file at default_path/filename

  Scenario (negative): Reserved prefix
    Given an object path starting with objects/ or s/
    When NormalizeObjectPath runs
    Then it rejects the path
